js 
js- js is used to add dynamic nature to the webpages
hoisting- declaration of a variable is moved to top before the
         execution
var ,let ,const - 
 var - redeclare,reassign,hoisting,scopes
 let - cannot redeclare,reassign,hoisting not possible(tdz)
 const -  cannot redeclare,cannot reassign, not possile (tdz)

  scope-accessibility of an variable
  block- let,const
  function- var,let ,const
  global-var,let ,const

datatypes
1) primitive - number,string,boolean ,undefined and null
2) non primitive- functions,array,objects,date 

functions- reusable block of code to perform specific task
          when something invokes it
types of functions
1) named function
2) arrow functions- concise way of writing a function-return,(),{}
3) anonymous function-a function that defines without a name 
4) callback funcions-when a function definition is passed to 
                  another func as an argument 

closure-
when an inner function remember and change the variable which are 
defined in outer function

synchronous js- which executes line by line
asynchronous js - parallel level of execution
1) promises- 
it specifies the eventual completion or failure of an asycnchronous operation

three state-
pending
resolved
rejected

creating a promise
consuming a promise 
1) .then.catch
2) async await



